---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Layout
  title="Documentation"
  description="Get started with Voice Inbox and find setup, testing, privacy, and troubleshooting guidance."
>
  <section class="section intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Voice Inbox documentation</p>
    <h1>From audio files to a local text inbox.</h1>
    <p>
      Voice Inbox is designed for accumulated recordings, not live dictation. Install a speech model,
      choose where transcripts are written, add audio files, then transcribe when you are ready.
    </p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button primary" href={`${base}/setup/`}>Open setup guide</a>
      <a class="button" href={`${base}/faq/`}>Browse FAQ</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <h2>1. Set up Voice Inbox</h2>
        <p>Install or download a compatible model, create or select an output document, and import audio.</p>
        <a href={`${base}/setup/`}>Read the setup guide →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h2>2. Get answers</h2>
        <p>Find help with device requirements, audio files, model installation, transcripts, and failures.</p>
        <a href={`${base}/faq/`}>Read the FAQ →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h2>3. Join testing</h2>
        <p>Voice Inbox for Android is currently distributed through Google Play closed testing.</p>
        <a href={`${base}/testing/`}>Read testing instructions →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>Learn how local transcription, downloaded models, and selected files work.</p>
        <a href={`${base}/privacy/`}>Read privacy information →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h2>Legal and acknowledgements</h2>
        <p>Review app information, source licensing, third-party notices, and model attribution.</p>
        <a href={`${base}/legal/`}>Read legal information →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section note">
    <h2>Platform notes</h2>
    <p>
      Android has the broader workflow today, including individual imports and sharing, optional folder
      processing, and scheduled transcription. iOS is an active MVP with local import, model installation,
      preview, transcription, and text output; its automation features are still evolving.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .intro { max-width: 760px; }
    .intro h1 { margin-bottom: 22px; }
    .intro p { font-size: 1.08rem; }
    .card h2 { font-size: 1.18rem; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  </style>
</Layout>
